    "number": 5,
    "total_in_level": 9,
    "title": "Nouns, Articles and Adjectives",
    "subtitle": "Gender, plurals, el / la / un / una, and how adjectives agree with the noun",
    "footer": "Spanish Learning Program · A1 · Grammar · Nouns, articles, adjectives",
    "next": "Next: A1 · PDF 6 — Pronouns, possessives and demonstratives"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "After this PDF you can",
      "bullets": [
        "guess the gender of most nouns from their ending, and learn the exceptions",
        "form regular plurals, including the spelling changes",
        "use el, la, los, las, un, una, unos, unas, al and del",
        "make adjectives agree with the noun and put them in the right place"
      ]
    },

    { "type": "h1", "text": "1. Gender of nouns" },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Every Spanish noun is <b>masculine</b> or <b>feminine</b>. There is no neuter. Learn each noun <b>together with its article</b>: <i>el libro, la mesa</i>."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [4.6, 6.0, 6.4],
      "head": ["Ending", "Usually", "Examples"],
      "rows": [
        ["-o", "masculine", "el libro, el coche, el vaso"],
        ["-a", "feminine", "la casa, la mesa, la ventana"],
        ["-ción, -sión, -dad, -tad, -tud", "feminine", "la canción, la televisión, la ciudad, la libertad"],
        ["-aje, -or, -án", "masculine", "el viaje, el color, el plan"],
        ["-ma (Greek words)", "masculine", "el problema, el tema, el sistema, el idioma, el programa"],
        ["-e or a consonant", "no rule: learn with the article", "el coche, la noche, el lápiz, la luz, el mes"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "verbpairs",
      "title": "Exceptions worth memorising",
      "items": [
        ["el día", "the day (masculine)"], ["el mapa", "the map (masculine)"], ["la mano", "the hand (feminine)"],
        ["la foto", "the photo (feminine)"], ["la moto", "the motorbike (feminine)"], ["el planeta", "the planet (masculine)"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "<b>People:</b> many nouns change the ending: <i>niño / niña, profesor / profesora, vecino / vecina</i>. Nouns in <b>-e</b>, <b>-ista</b> and many others stay the same and only the article shows the gender: <i>el / la estudiante, el / la turista, el / la dentista</i>."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "dutch",
      "title": "Dutch de / het does not map onto el / la",
      "text": "Do not guess the gender from the Dutch noun. <i>Het meisje</i> is <b>la</b> chica, <i>de zon</i> is <b>el</b> sol, <i>de maan</i> is <b>la</b> luna. Learn each Spanish noun with its article."
    },

    { "type": "h1", "text": "2. Plural of nouns" },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [5.4, 3.0, 4.0, 4.6],
      "head": ["Singular ends in", "Add", "Singular", "Plural"],
      "rows": [
        ["an unstressed vowel", "-s", "la casa, el coche", "las casas, los coches"],
        ["a stressed vowel (á, é, ó)", "-s (or -es)", "el café, el sofá", "los cafés, los sofás"],
        ["a consonant", "-es", "la ciudad, el papel", "las ciudades, los papeles"],
        ["-z", "-ces (z becomes c)", "el lápiz, la vez", "los lápices, las veces"],
        ["-ción, -sión (drop the accent)", "-ones", "la canción", "las canciones"],
        ["-s after an unstressed syllable", "no change", "el lunes, el paraguas", "los lunes, los paraguas"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "Watch the accent when the word grows",
      "text": "<b>canción to canciones</b> loses its accent. <b>examen to exámenes</b> and <b>joven to jóvenes</b> gain one. <b>país to países</b> and <b>autobús to autobuses</b> keep the stress where it was. The rule from PDF 1 (stress and accents) decides each time."
    },

    { "type": "h1", "text": "3. Articles" },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [4.0, 3.2, 3.2, 3.3, 3.3],
      "head": ["", "masculine sing.", "feminine sing.", "masculine pl.", "feminine pl."],
      "rows": [
        ["definite (the)", "el", "la", "los", "las"],
        ["indefinite (a, an / some)", "un", "una", "unos", "unas"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "<b>Contractions:</b> a + el = <b>al</b>, de + el = <b>del</b>. <i>Voy al mercado. Es el libro del profesor.</i> (No contraction with la, los, las, or with the name <i>El</i> Salvador.)",
        "<b>el with a feminine noun:</b> a feminine singular noun that starts with a stressed a- takes <i>el</i>, but stays feminine: <i>el agua fría, el águila</i>. The plural is regular: <i>las aguas</i>.",
        "<b>Days:</b> <i>el lunes</i> (on Monday), <i>los lunes</i> (on Mondays). <b>Time:</b> <i>la una, las dos</i>.",
        "<b>No article</b> after ser with a profession: <i>Soy médico.</i> And with a language that you speak: <i>Hablo español.</i> But <i>El español es fácil.</i> (the language is the subject)",
        "<b>unos / unas</b> mean “some” or “a few”: <i>unos amigos</i>."
      ]
    },

    { "type": "h1", "text": "4. Adjectives agree with the noun" },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "An adjective matches its noun in <b>gender</b> and <b>number</b>: <i>un chico alto, una chica alta, unos chicos altos, unas chicas altas</i>. It normally goes <b>after</b> the noun."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [4.2, 3.2, 3.2, 3.2, 3.2],
      "head": ["Type", "masc. sing.", "fem. sing.", "masc. pl.", "fem. pl."],
      "rows": [
        ["-o adjectives", "alto", "alta", "altos", "altas"],
        ["-e or consonant", "grande, fácil", "grande, fácil", "grandes, fáciles", "grandes, fáciles"],
        ["nationality in a consonant", "español", "española", "españoles", "españolas"],
        ["-dor, -ón, -és, -án", "trabajador", "trabajadora", "trabajadores", "trabajadoras"],
        ["colour: -e or consonant", "verde, azul", "verde, azul", "verdes, azules", "verdes, azules"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "verbpairs",
      "title": "Nationalities (masculine / feminine)",
      "items": [
        ["español / española", "Spanish"], ["inglés / inglesa", "English"], ["alemán / alemana", "German"], ["francés / francesa", "French"],
        ["holandés / holandesa", "Dutch"], ["italiano / italiana", "Italian"], ["portugués / portuguesa", "Portuguese"], ["estadounidense", "American (same for both)"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "verbpairs",
      "title": "Common adjectives",
      "items": [
        ["grande / pequeño", "big / small"], ["alto / bajo", "tall / short"], ["nuevo / viejo", "new / old"], ["bueno / malo", "good / bad"],
        ["fácil / difícil", "easy / difficult"], ["caro / barato", "expensive / cheap"], ["rápido / lento", "fast / slow"], ["simpático / antipático", "nice / unpleasant"],
        ["guapo / feo", "good-looking / ugly"], ["joven / mayor", "young / older"], ["rico / pobre", "rich / poor"], ["feliz / triste", "happy / sad"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "verbpairs",
      "title": "Colours",
      "items": [
        ["rojo", "red"], ["azul", "blue"], ["verde", "green"], ["amarillo", "yellow"],
        ["negro", "black"], ["blanco", "white"], ["gris", "grey"], ["marrón", "brown"],
        ["naranja", "orange"], ["rosa", "pink"], ["morado", "purple"], ["dorado", "golden"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "<b>bueno</b> and <b>malo</b> lose the final -o before a masculine singular noun: <i>un buen día, un mal día</i> (but <i>una buena idea</i>).",
        "<b>Numbers and quantity</b> go before the noun: <i>dos libros, muchos amigos, poco tiempo</i>.",
        "<b>Colours</b> go after the noun: <i>un coche rojo, una casa blanca</i>."
      ]
    },

    { "type": "h1", "text": "5. Common mistakes" },
    {
      "type": "mistakes",
      "rows": [
        ["la problema", "el problema", "Words in -ma from Greek are masculine."],
        ["una libro", "un libro", "libro is masculine, so un."],
        ["las casas blanco", "las casas blancas", "The adjective agrees in gender and number."],
        ["un coche roja", "un coche rojo", "coche is masculine, so rojo."],
        ["una chica simpático", "una chica simpática", "Feminine noun, feminine adjective."],
        ["Hablo el español.", "Hablo español.", "No article after verbs like hablar, estudiar or aprender with a language."],
        ["un rojo coche", "un coche rojo", "Colours and most adjectives go after the noun."],
        ["los lápizes", "los lápices", "z becomes c before -es."]
      ]
    },

    { "type": "h1", "text": "6. Self-check" },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Complete each sentence. Answers are on the last page."
    },
    {
      "type": "exercises",
      "titles": ["Sentence", "Task"],
      "items": [
        { "q": "______ problema es difícil.", "hint": "the", "a": "El", "full": "El problema es difícil." },
        { "q": "Quiero ______ café.", "hint": "a", "a": "un", "full": "Quiero un café." },
        { "q": "______ casas son grandes.", "hint": "the (plural)", "a": "Las", "full": "Las casas son grandes." },
        { "q": "Tengo dos ______.", "hint": "libro (plural)", "a": "libros", "full": "Tengo dos libros." },
        { "q": "Es una casa ______.", "hint": "blanco", "a": "blanca", "full": "Es una casa blanca." },
        { "q": "Mis amigos son ______.", "hint": "simpático", "a": "simpáticos", "full": "Mis amigos son simpáticos." },
        { "q": "______ agua está fría.", "hint": "the", "a": "El", "full": "El agua está fría." },
        { "q": "Voy ______ supermercado.", "hint": "a + el", "a": "al", "full": "Voy al supermercado." },
        { "q": "Los ______ de la clase están en la mesa.", "hint": "lápiz (plural)", "a": "lápices", "full": "Los lápices de la clase están en la mesa." },
        { "q": "Hay muchas ______ en el concierto.", "hint": "canción (plural)", "a": "canciones", "full": "Hay muchas canciones en el concierto." },
        { "q": "Es un ______ día.", "hint": "bueno", "a": "buen", "full": "Es un buen día." },
        { "q": "Las flores son ______.", "hint": "rojo", "a": "rojas", "full": "Las flores son rojas." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "<b>Translate into Spanish:</b>"
    },
    {
      "type": "translations",
      "items": [
